From 38bb67de9bb7194c8632b86781b08de6a166962a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:50:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08051/11362] The induce headline was pseudo-replicated, and
 the spec never learned the module got wired

Adversarial review of the induce-reliability Phases 1-3 returned 15 findings. All 15 verified
against the run's own data before being applied; none were wrong; all 15 applied. No GPU time --
a concurrent best-of-N run held GPU 1 throughout and its files were left untouched.

THE HEADLINE THAT OPENED THE PHASE 2 GATE WAS INFLATED TWICE.

"triples the rate of valid engines" -- the note title and the immutable subject of 463f81075.
No measured rate triples: usable 13/36 -> 22/36 is 1.69x, penalty-alone 1.54x, and the most
generous framing available (defect-free 14/36 -> 29/36) is 2.07x. The body always had it right,
so the error lived entirely in the most-propagated string. H1 amended; the commit subject cannot
be, which is why the correction is in ops/changelog.md too.

p = 0.049 is pseudo-replicated. The 36 pairs are 6 games x 6 resamples of ONE prompt each, but
the sign test treated all 17 discordant pairs as independent. Clustered at the game level -- the
unit that generalizes to an unseen game -- it is p = 0.125 (4 better, 0 worse, 2 tied); a
whole-game sign-flip permutation test agrees exactly (net +9, p = 0.1250). With 6 games the
reachable floor is 2/2^6 = 0.031, so significance required all six to improve. The wiring
decision still stands, on the consistent direction and a cost effect large enough to need no
test -- not on a p.

AND THE QUALITY NULL IS SHARPER THAN THE NOTE ADMITTED.

Restricted to the three games whose held-out set contains a CHANGING transition, strict quality
is 4 of 18 attempts in EVERY arm -- identical. The entire 2/6 -> 3/6 strict-funnel gain is ft09,
which has zero held-out changing rows and passes only on the weaker no-op fallback. Both
components were disclosed; the conjunction never was, and it is the result: the treatment
produced no better engine on any game where change prediction could be graded.

TWO STRUCTURAL DEFECTS IN SHIPPED SCOPE.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6052 still said "the shipped induce path is UNCHANGED; nothing calls it" -- false
since 7d7c71a49. That session removed the orphan-lint allow-list entry whose own comment read
"Retire this entry when the module is wired" and never updated the spec it pointed at. Amended
additively. REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-41, cited by shipped source and its test, did not exist anywhere in
openspec (highest was -39); now written with 5 scenarios and an Implementation Status row.

repeat_penalty was shipping to a call it was never measured on: the gate was codeonly_eligible
alone, which is also True for _split_induce's goal-only call. Narrowed to match the defect gate.
Conservative direction -- with no measurement either way that call's correct state is the
no-penalty baseline every banked result was produced under. Both mutations killed.

ARTIFACT REPAIRS, DIFFED LEAF BY LEAF.

confirm_scored.json failed adversarial_verify with METHODOLOGY_MISSING while the Phase 3 artifact
was fully compliant -- the discipline had been applied unevenly inside one session. Now carries
all five fields; 0 flagged. Regenerated and diffed: 3009 -> 3248 leaves, 0 removed, exactly two
changed (run_date, and the min_reachable_p_two_sided bug itself, which reported 0.0 at 17
discordant pairs -- a value no test can attain). No measurement moved.

split.json advertised a tautology as a check: no_heldout_line_in_prompt was the literal True,
"true by construction". Replaced with an independent post-hoc assertion plus a counting identity;
mutation-verified -- keeping ambiguous rows flips it False, where the old code stayed True.

The shared-server-process property was asserted, not measured: server_pid was captured once per
worker, and Phase 3 later proved the failure mode real. Per-call read and scorer guard
retrofitted; the 72 existing pairs are recorded UNVERIFIED rather than reported clean.

Phase 1 also scored the wrong induce call site (CONFIRM_CALL_INDEX defaults to 2; the gates and
_proposal_prefix live on call 1, where ft09 has 4 held-out changing rows against 0), and pinned
n_ctx=32768 while the shipped default is 81920. Both now disclosed and scoped.

THE NEAR-MISS: TWO REBUILDS RAN AGAINST THE WRONG SOURCE.

The narrowing re-staled the same 7 artifacts. Same outcome as Phase 2 -- 0 substantive movement
across 77,543 compared leaves, sole exception 6012's reproducibility_checksum, a hash OVER the
dependency set -- so all 7 discharged by acknowledgement, +8 -0 on every file, zero deletions.
But a concurrent process reverted the working tree mid-sequence (source and both notes rolled
back to HEAD while the INDEX kept the staged content), so two rebuilds ran against the PRE-change
source and would have been written up as evidence for a change they never exercised. Caught by
reading each rebuild's own provenance.code sha rather than trusting the file on disk; invalid
rebuilds rerun, and every acknowledgement cites that check. After a failed pre-commit run, verify
the working tree still matches the index before trusting anything measured afterwards.

25 test failures are pre-existing -- verified by differential, reverting only the source change:
zero regressions, and the single delta is the new narrowing test correctly failing at HEAD.
Harness formatting debt was also pre-existing and surfaced only by staging; the reformat is
proven inert by re-running the scorer (only run_date moved).

